  "final_message": "The task to list git files has been launched, waiting for the results...\nRunning test suite...\nChecking codebase for ARCH-4 references...\nChecking for deprecation references...\nChecking usages of channel...\nI cannot directly remove the `channel` field from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/GEMINI.md#L28-L34).\n\n### Architectural Conflict: ARCH-4\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n1. **Breaking External Consumers**: [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is published to Kafka (`orders.placed`) and consumed by independent services in external repositories (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Removing `channel` is a non-additive, breaking schema change.\n2. **Order Model Dependency**: Removing `channel` from the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) entity prevents [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) from populating the event contract.\n3. **Deprecation Requirement**: Under ARCH-4, field removals cannot happen abruptly in a single step; they must undergo a formal deprecation lifecycle across services.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Deprecation Path\n\nTo safely retire `channel` in compliance with architecture governance:\n\n1. **Deprecate the Field**: Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` on [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L16), [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L23), and [`NewOrder`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L35) without removing it.\n2. **Make Optional on Ingestion (if desired)**: Allow [`parsePlaceOrderRequest`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/api/requestParsing.ts#L11-L41) to default `channel` when omitted, while continuing to publish a valid fallback value in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26).\n3. **Migrate Downstream Consumers**: Announce deprecation and ensure `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest` deploy updates removing any dependency on `channel`.\n4. **Coordinated Schema Evolution**: Once downstream consumers are updated, introduce the removal under a coordinated schema version bump (e.g., `OrderPlaced` schema version 4).\n",
